  "id": "DrugBank_DB00901 - MONDO_4849",
  "verbalization": "Bitolterol is implicated in the pathogenesis of Pulmonary Emphysema through a series of indirect pathways involving respiratory conditions. The evidence suggests that Bitolterol is associated with Bronchiectasis and Bronchitis, which in turn are linked to Pulmonary Emphysema via the use of Pirbuterol and Tiotropium, respectively. These bronchodilators are known to exert effects on airway remodeling and inflammation, which may contribute to the progression of emphysema. The cumulative evidence points to a potential role of Bitolterol in the development of Pulmonary Emphysema through its influence on respiratory conditions that are mechanistically linked to the disease. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on bronchodilator use in the context of respiratory disease progression, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
